The transcript will be in the form of a series of lines. Each line is a chunk of text that was said by a speaker in the meeting.
Each line includes the line number which should be used for reference.
Each line is separated by a new line character.
The default format for a line is `line n: speaker_name: speaker_text`
The speaker_name is optional and may not always be presented, so the format can also be `line n: speaker_text`

Example:

line 1: Bob Clams: Hello, how are you?
line 2: Alice: I'm good, how are you?
line 3: Hi everyone!

Explanation:
In this example line 1 has a speaker name of Bob Clams and speaker text of "Hello, how are you?"
line 2 has a speaker name of Alice and speaker text of "I'm good, how are you?"
line 3 has no speaker name and the speaker text is "Hi everyone!"

You should always use the line number to reference a line in the transcript.
